      "summary": "Per §3.2.4 brief, removing the HOST_PARSED_*_CACHE thread-locals required removing their consumer behaviour. Brief said 'consumers fall back to direct compute and store the result in the DB on first use' but the empty 1A typed DBs store `Arc<OwnedEvalProgram>` (Send+Sync+'static) while consumers still produce the borrowed `Rc<ParsedEvalProgram>` types — the types don't match. Resolution: removed the cache fully (per-call ParsedEvalProgram::parse). Performance regression is intentional and bounded to 1A; 1C-α adds back warm-cache behaviour through the typed DB once consumers migrate to `OwnedEvalProgram`.",
